WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.167
IEC 62443 is a family of standards for industrial automation and control system cybersecurity.

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:16.860
It connects organizational programs, risk assessment, system architecture, product capabilities, service responsibilities, and lifecycle operation.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:21.865
It is not a single checklist or product.

00:00:21.865 --> 00:00:26.344
Responsibilities are shared but must remain explicit.

00:00:26.344 --> 00:00:31.349
Asset owners define risk and sustain the program.

00:00:31.349 --> 00:00:35.300
Integrators implement and verify secure systems.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:40.833
Product suppliers provide secure development practices and component capabilities.

00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:46.365
Service providers maintain access and changes within approved controls.

00:00:46.365 --> 00:00:50.843
Zones group assets with related security requirements.

00:00:50.843 --> 00:00:54.795
Conduits control communication between those zones.

00:00:54.795 --> 00:01:07.703
Security levels translate risk into protection expectations, while the foundational requirements organize identity, use, integrity, confidentiality, restricted flow, event response, and availability objectives.

00:01:07.703 --> 00:01:12.181
Successful implementation depends on evidence and engineering.

00:01:12.181 --> 00:01:28.251
Inventory assets, understand the process, assess risk, configure capabilities, test controls, govern remote access, monitor meaningful activity, maintain backups, control changes, and plan for incident recovery and technology retirement.

00:01:28.251 --> 00:01:33.256
The central lesson is collaboration across the lifecycle.

00:01:33.256 --> 00:01:42.477
IEC 62443 gives engineering, operations, cybersecurity, suppliers, and management a common structure for making defensible decisions.

00:01:42.477 --> 00:01:52.751
The official standards and environment-specific analysis provide the detail; disciplined ownership turns that detail into resilient industrial operations.
